Your command requires Docker Desktop’s Linux engine to be running. 
When Docker Desktop is closed, still starting, or its WSL backend has stopped, 
Docker cannot access:
````
    \\.\pipe\dockerDesktopLinuxEngine

Before running Compose, you can check it with:
`````
    docker info

If it reports the same named-pipe error, start Docker Desktop and wait until it shows that the engine is running. You can also start it from PowerShell:

`````
    Start-Process "C:\Program Files\Docker\Docker\Docker Desktop.exe"

    Then verify:

````
    docker context use desktop-linux
    docker info 